  "body": "Tucked into a quiet pocket of Kohimarama, this two-level executive-style home has been thoughtfully updated. Everyday living gathers around a private, covered deck and a bushy setting of trees and ferns. Convenient, easy to look after, and a pleasure to come home to.\r\n\r\nA quiet sitting room sits beside the entry. The open-plan kitchen, dining, living and family rooms flow together beneath a double-height volume. Stacking doors open to the covered outdoor room and the greenery beyond.\r\n\r\nThe kitchen has been carefully updated, with white cabinetry, a dark stone island, timber floors, a stainless splashback, gas cooktop, dishwasher and Bosch double wall ovens. A gold mosaic feature wall adds warmth to the living space. Central heating and a living-area heat pump keep the home comfortable year-round.\r\n\r\nOutside, a covered, louvred-pergola terrace looks into trees and ferns, a natural place for morning coffee and quiet evenings.\r\n\r\n* Three bedrooms upstairs, including a master with a walk-in wardrobe and ensuite, and a well-presented family bathroom with a bath. The third bedroom works readily as a home office. A guest WC and a separate laundry with outdoor access sit on the ground floor.\r\n\r\n* Secure parking is a breeze with a double internal-access garage and up to two additional off-street parks.\r\n\r\nSt Thomas's School is just around the corner, with Selwyn College close by. The Allum Street shops, including Forbes, are a short stroll away. Madills Farm, Kohimarama Beach and the cafes of Tamaki Drive are an easy walk.\r\n\r\nOur vendors have loved living here, and have now decided to make Pauanui their home. They are ready for someone else to enjoy it, as they have. Your earliest inspection is recommended. \r\n\r\nCall Team Frazer MJ Today.",
